DOCKERFILE: Has some set of instructions which help run applications. It should have code for docker image, libraries which help 
operate the application, should have information of the operating system to be used, should have information of framework/tools/repositories/libraries.

DOCKERFILE for Java application

# pull a base image which provides all required tools and libraries 
FROM openjdk:17-jdk-alpine            #Google official Java runtime base image, 17 is tag, jdk-alpine is lightweight

#create a folder where the app code will be stored
WORKDIR /app                               # Destination

#Copy the source code from host machine to your container
COPY . .                                  # copy in current directory  
#or COPY src/Main.java app/Main.java

#Compile the application code
RUN javac src/Main.java                   #java first compiles and then run the application 
# or RUN Main.java

#run the application code
CMD ["java", "Main"]                    #ENTRYPOINT["java", "MAIN"]  Entrypoint does not make it overwritable

