Dockerfile for python application (flask-app-ecs)
Check all the requirements.txt file, src file etc

FROM python:3.7         #base image


WORKDIR /app            #working directory, flask app runs on port 80


COPY . .


RUN pip install -r requirements.txt        #check how to install requirements of python application


CMD ["python", "run.py"]                   #or ENTRYPOINT ["python"]
                                           #CMD ["run.py"]

Note:
Flask app runs on port 80

host port and container port

Port mapping allows you to connect your local machine (Host) to the software running inside Docker (Container). 
By default, containers are isolated; ports must be explicitly "opened" to access them from your browser or terminal.

